{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b696-3f99-7152-9387-7f894ec27196","session_id":"01a1b694-bf86-79ef-9b9d-323d8d10c8a2","message":{"id":"01a1b6963f99715293877f87976e7811","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand the situation better. The live.json says I'm role=review, round=1, model=hy4std. So I'm being invoked as \"review\" round 1 (a fresh review attempt in this worker session). The previous review-r1.md / verdict-r1.json were written by a different model (gpt-6-astra) that produced needs_revision. Actually wait — the run.json shows review round 1 candidate 1 (gpt-6-astra) completed at 14:50:30 with exit 0 — that's the review-r1.md content. Then dev round 2 (grok-4.7) made changes, then CI re-ran at 15:05:53, then review round 2 candidate 1 (gpt-6-astra) stalled at 15:13:59, then CI re-ran at 15:16:02, and now I'm invoked.\n\nBut live.json says round=1. Hmm, that's confusing. live.json started_at 15:16:02.459Z which matches the last CI run. So this current invocation is fresh, labeled round 1 (maybe the harness restarted the round counter, or this is a new \"worker\" attempt).\n\nRegardless: my output should be review.md or review-r1.md, verdict.json or verdict-r1.json. Given that review-r1.md and verdict-r1.json already exist with the previous reviewer's conclusion, and I'm doing a NEW review of the CURRENT state (after dev r2 changes), I think the cleanest is to write `review.md` and `verdict.json` (the unsuffixed names) — these don't exist yet, so I'm creating them, not overwriting the previous round's artifacts. Actually, hmm, but \"produce review.md or review-r1.md\" — both are allowed. Since r1 files exist from the previous reviewer, writing them would overwrite history. But the instruction says \"若 brief 指定了验收报告路径，把本轮结论追加到该文档（不要改历史小节）\" — don't modify historical sections. That's about the acceptance report, not the review file. \n\nHmm, actually, let me think. The safest interpretation: I can create either pair. Since review-r1.md/verdict-r