ght read the OLD ones and think I did nothing.\n\nHmm. Let me think about this more. live.json says round: 1. The harness likely expects review-r1.md and verdict-r1.json for round 1. But those already exist. The instruction explicitly allows \"review.md 或 review-r1.md\" — \"或\" (or) means either. Given that the r1 files exist from a previous stalled/completed attempt, and the task says \"产出：review.md 或 review-r1.md\" — I think the intent is: write to whichever naming convention applies. The existence of r1 files suggests the harness expects review-r1.md. Overwriting them is \"修改\" which is explicitly allowed (\"只能创建或修改这些文件\"). \n\nActually — I think the cleanest and safest is to write to BOTH the r1 files (overwrite with my current conclusion) AND... no, that's redundant.\n\nLet me re-read: \"产出：review.md 或 review-r1.md、verdict.json 或 verdict-r1.json（只能创建或修改这些文件）\". I think this is giving me flexibility because the harness doesn't know which round naming I'll use. The \"或\" lets me choose. I'll choose `review.md` and `verdict.json` to avoid overwriting prior round artifacts... \n\nHmm, but actually, wait. Let me reconsider once more. The previous review-r1.md says \"本轮仅创建 review-r1.md、verdict-r1.json\". So that reviewer created those. If I'm now doing a subsequent review of the same task (after dev fixed things), the natural thing is to create review-r2.md/verdict-r2.json — but those aren't allowed. So the harness must be telling me to either use the generic names (review.md/verdict.json) or overwrite r1. \n\nGiven the explicit \"只能创建或修改这些文件\" and \"review.md 或 review-r1.md\", I'll go with writing to `review.md` and `verdict.json` AND also updating `review-r1.md` and `verdict-r1.json`? That would be 4 files. Hmm, that seems excessive but ensures the harness picks up my conclusion regardless of which name it reads. Actually — but overwriting r1 with a different verdict could be seen as \"改历史小节\" (modifying historical sections), which the instruction warns against for